{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1000608-mage-intelligence","id":1000608,"title":"Mage intelligence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-08T21:42:13-08:00","id":1000608,"title":"Mage intelligence","content":"Obviously there is not an intelligence requirement in Mage the way there is one for wizards in D&amp;D. I still find it hard to imagine a Mage who's not even a bit smarter than average--it seems like even an atavistic Primordial-Essence Mage would tend to have a kind of clarity and cunning that would put them squarely on the right half of the bell curve. Understanding any kind of paradigm well enough to Awaken would seem to require some intelligence. So I make players take a minimum of 3. Does anyone else do the same? Does anyone else have good examples of Mage characters they've seen or played with an Intelligence of 2 or 1?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","user":"Faradn","date":". 11-09-2016, 07:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T23:18:48-08:00","id":1000624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1000608-mage-intelligence#post1000608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously there is not intelligence requirement in Mage the way there is one for wizards in D&amp;D. I still find it hard to imagine a Mage who's not even a bit smarter than average--it seems like even an atavistic Primordial-Essence Mage would tend to have a kind of clarity and cunning that would put them squarely on the right half of the bell curve. Understanding any kind of paradigm well enough to Awaken would seem to require some intelligence. So I make players take a minimum of 3. Does anyone else do the same? Does anyone else have good examples of Mage characters they've seen or played with an Intelligence of 2 or 1?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I agree with you completelly. Not only for mages, but also Blood Sorcerers, Occultists and the like, I require a minimun of 3 dots of Intellgence. To imagine a Mage with Inteligence 1 or even 2 seems pathethic to me. I have already gone as far as to force a player who was roleplaying too strategically (he's a military commander) to use his xp to increase his Inteligence rating. I really hate the idea of a player roleplaying genial stratagems in the game without the equivalent trait in game. As for mages and deep thinkers the journey only begins at 3.<br /> <br /> Cheers,<br /> Daniel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T00:43:01-08:00","id":1000647,"title":"","content":"I don't think a mage has to be above average in Intelligence, though I could be convinced that they should be above average in either Intelligence or Wits.<br /> <br /> Not every Focus actually requires you to be smart. You don't have to be a Hermetic that studies a dozen tomes to learn how to construct summoning sigils just right. What does a Chorister that spends most of their time doing charity work with some magical boosts to aid the ill and needy actually need above average Intelligence for? They don't need an encyclopedic knowledge of prayers to bring the light of the One to the masses. They don't need problem solving skills for things like, &quot;this guy is starving so I'm going to 'find' some food over here.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd agree that being smarter than average is quite common among mages (it's important to plenty of magical styles, and mages get 7/5/3 Attributes at start which means the default assumption is that they're already exceptional people), but I can think of lots of avenues for characters where the Intelligence stat is not vital to the concept being executed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T00:51:46-08:00","id":1000650,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's really anything in Mage: The Ascension that requires a high intelligence score. This seems to me to be a bias based on how things are run in D&amp;D (which is great for D&amp;D, don't get me wrong), but it doesn't necessarily apply to Mage. Enlightenment isn't a function of your IQ but more a matter of outlook.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't demand a minimum intelligence for any Mage characters.<br /> <br /> Also, what Heavy Arms said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T01:23:36-08:00","id":1000661,"title":"","content":"There are Archetypes recommending a moderate to high Intelligence: The Hermetic, the Etherist, the V-dept and their typical styles (High Ritual, Science!, Hacking)<br /> <br /> But Shamanism, Witchcraft, Do and several others do not require it.<br /> And keep in mind, that 2 is average. That means a lot of techies, scientists and teachers have \u201conly\u201c intelligence 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T02:01:45-08:00","id":1000667,"title":"","content":"And really, average intelligence for humans is quite intelligent, overall. It gets short shrift for being average but it's nothing to sneeze at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T04:05:52-08:00","id":1000696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1000608-mage-intelligence?p=1000647#post1000647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think a mage has to be above average in Intelligence, though I could be convinced that they should be above average in either Intelligence or Wits.<br /> <br /> Not every Focus actually requires you to be smart. You don't have to be a Hermetic that studies a dozen tomes to learn how to construct summoning sigils just right. What does a Chorister that spends most of their time doing charity work with some magical boosts to aid the ill and needy actually need above average Intelligence for? They don't need an encyclopedic knowledge of prayers to bring the light of the One to the masses. They don't need problem solving skills for things like, &quot;this guy is starving so I'm going to 'find' some food over here.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd agree that being smarter than average is quite common among mages (it's important to plenty of magical styles, and mages get 7/5/3 Attributes at start which means the default assumption is that they're already exceptional people), but I can think of lots of avenues for characters where the Intelligence stat is not vital to the concept being executed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Good points. I see that for the general &quot;miracle worker&quot;, inteligence isn't that much of a requirement, so for that archetype it does make sense having a trait of 2 (or even &quot;omg duh&quot; intelligence 1) and still &quot;meet the requirement&quot;. In any case, I think that overall it's very cheesy for many kinds of characters to think intelligence 2 should be enough to get everything they want in game (players tend to not give a good priority to purchase attribube points with xp), besides, Inteligence 2 is basically around (according to the books at least) Iq 100 or so, don't get me wrong, but it's a bit hard for me to imagine many teachers with such low iq, let alone &quot;Wizards who can bend the laws of reality itself&quot;.<br /> <br /> Cheers,<br /> Daniel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 11-09-2016, 07:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T05:01:04-08:00","id":1000705,"title":"","content":"I would suggest that most professionals have their central Attribute at 3, with 4 or 5 becoming progressively rarer. An 'average' starting mortal can have 8 dice in their field (Attribute 3 plus Ability 5) without exceptional Attributes, though I would think that most professionals would do fine with 6 dice (Attribute 3 plus Ability 3). That would give good performance (2.4 successes) on difficulty 6 tasks, with a chance of succeeding (1.2 successes) on difficult 8 tasks. It also gives them a small probability for sheer brilliance (5 successes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T05:11:53-08:00","id":1000708,"title":"","content":"I tend to find that Mages don't need actual dots in Intelligence to turn out near-genius level intellectual tasks; the potency of 1- &amp; 2-dot Spheres as tools for mental modelling, anticipation &amp; insight leave any 'natural' intelligence in the dust.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T11:34:43-08:00","id":1000910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1000608-mage-intelligence?p=1000647#post1000647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think a mage has to be above average in Intelligence, though I could be convinced that they should be above average in either Intelligence or Wits.<br /> <br /> Not every Focus actually requires you to be smart. You don't have to be a Hermetic that studies a dozen tomes to learn how to construct summoning sigils just right. What does a Chorister that spends most of their time doing charity work with some magical boosts to aid the ill and needy actually need above average Intelligence for? They don't need an encyclopedic knowledge of prayers to bring the light of the One to the masses. They don't need problem solving skills for things like, &quot;this guy is starving so I'm going to 'find' some food over here.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd agree that being smarter than average is quite common among mages (it's important to plenty of magical styles, and mages get 7/5/3 Attributes at start which means the default assumption is that they're already exceptional people), but I can think of lots of avenues for characters where the Intelligence stat is not vital to the concept being executed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really agree with what Heavy Arms on this one. While I do think a Mage needs to be intelligent I also think that a different focus can mean a different stat is needed. I can also see some styles using Social based stats or even Physical ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T11:50:41-08:00","id":1000917,"title":"","content":"The key to understanding the difference between DnD wizards (who, inter-narratively, are just very powerful hedge sorcerers, relative to Mage, who exist in an umbral realm that has metaphysics that support &quot;x&quot; paradigm of magic, thus empowering their hedge spells) and Mages, relative to &quot;Intelligence&quot;, is that one doesn't have to be bright or even of average intelligence in order to be Awakened. A (M)age may well have some form of mental handicap (from the &quot;milder&quot; forms of high-functioning mental retardation to severe learning disabilities that make conventional intellectualization nigh impossible, or even simply have Downs Syndrome, which can have variable effects on mental ability/acuity -- see Nan from AHS: Coven) but still be a mage just as his more intellectually gifted brethren might be, albeit in a different way. He may not be a, say, Hermetic, VA, SoE or similar, but he could easily be a DS/ST, a Verbena, or simply an Orphan of self-realized power (particularly if they happen to be the incarnation of a particularly powerful Avatar/Fount and/or have Dream, Past Lives, or similar; a more child-minded mage may even be quite adept at Wishcraft, thus obviating the need for more learned/practiced forms altogether). Seeing (M)ages solely through the lens of &quot;intelligence&quot; is in-and-of-itself a matter of applied (P)aradigm on the part of the *player*, not a limit in any real way for most character concepts of a &quot;less-than-average-smarts&quot; character. (Now, a seriously retarded individual -- IQ of 10-30 or so -- would often be a danger to himself and others if he Awakened; that, however, is a rare situation, and in most cases the character is either kept safe from harm by other mages or -- and this is the more likely of scenarios, harsh as it might be -- he will simply be &quot;put down&quot; before he becomes too much of a threat... assuming, of course, he doesn't 'dox/backlash himself out of existence first....)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T16:32:17-08:00","id":1001066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1000608-mage-intelligence?p=1000661#post1000661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are Archetypes recommending a moderate to high Intelligence: The Hermetic, the Etherist, the V-dept and their typical styles (High Ritual, Science!, Hacking)<br /> <br /> But Shamanism, Witchcraft, Do and several others do not require it.<br /> And keep in mind, that 2 is average. That means a lot of techies, scientists and teachers have \u201conly\u201c intelligence 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shamans are the intellectual elite of their cultures. &quot;Witches,&quot; at least competent ones, know a lot of herbal lore. There is a substantial intellectual component to martial arts.<br /> <br /> Heavy Arms mentioned a charity-minded Chorister, and I kind of get that. Except that almost anyone who does charity work on the level of organizing other people and making a large difference--aka anyone who is <i>exceptional</i> at what they are doing, as a mage should be--is going to be smarter than average.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T16:46:32-08:00","id":1001073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1000608-mage-intelligence?p=1000696#post1000696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Good points. I see that for the general &quot;miracle worker&quot;, inteligence isn't that much of a requirement, so for that archetype it does make sense having a trait of 2 (or even &quot;omg duh&quot; intelligence 1) and still &quot;meet the requirement&quot;. In any case, I think that overall it's very cheesy for many kinds of characters to think intelligence 2 should be enough to get everything they want in game (players tend to not give a good priority to purchase attribube points with xp), besides, Inteligence 2 is basically around (according to the books at least) Iq 100 or so, don't get me wrong, but it's a bit hard for me to imagine many teachers with such low iq, let alone &quot;Wizards who can bend the laws of reality itself&quot;.<br /> <br /> Cheers,<br /> Daniel.</div> </div> </div> </div>100 IQ isn't low, though. It's <i>average</i>, and average for humans is smarter than most people (like yourself) credit it to be.<br /> <br /> The ability to &quot;bend the laws of reality&quot; isn't an intellectual talent. There's no connection from <i>any</i> attribute to <i>the ability</i> to perform magick. A mage can reasonably have any spread of attribute dots based on 7/5/3 and that's perfectly fine.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T18:44:58-08:00","id":1001128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1000608-mage-intelligence?p=1001066#post1001066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shamans are the intellectual elite of their cultures.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Intellectual elite&quot; isn't the same as &quot;high Intelligence stat.&quot; Even getting beyond the specific cultural expertise, there are going to be people that rely more on innate talent (Attributes), people that rely on training (Abilities), and people that have a mix of both. The luminaries that have high ratings of both are exceptional.<br /> <br /> Scientists are a form of the intellectual elite, but most of them are not going to have more than Intelligence 2 and Science 3 allowing them to be competent scientists in any research lab even if they're not breaking ground with revolutionary hypotheses. <br /> <br /> There's also issues with the fact that &quot;being smart&quot; isn't the same as high Intelligence. Lots of &quot;smart people&quot; have been exceptional via Perception or Wits rather than Intelligence; especially in intellectual pursuits. One of the things about intellectual elites is that most of them have time to make up being not super-intelligent with hard work, but having the ability to notice the right thing at the right time can be career making. We don't have modern vaccines because of high Intelligence, but because of high Wits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is a substantial intellectual component to martial arts. </div> </div> </div>And how does the difference between an IQ of 100 and an IQ of 120 matter to that component?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Heavy Arms mentioned a charity-minded Chorister, and I kind of get that. Except that almost anyone who does charity work on the level of organizing other people and making a large difference--aka anyone who is <i>exceptional</i> at what they are doing, as a mage should be--is going to be smarter than average. </div> </div> </div>But that's not actually &quot;getting&quot; my example. My example wasn't a community organizer, or the head of a charity, but simple a person that goes around doing good works.<br /> <br /> As well, a lot of leaders are not the smartest person in their organization. Many good leaders are effective because of their ability to find smarter people that are good for specific tasks and the ability to judge character and skill is far more important than problem solving and memory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T22:44:38-08:00","id":1001207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1000608-mage-intelligence?p=1001073#post1001073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 100 IQ isn't low, though. It's <i>average</i>, and average for humans is smarter than most people (like yourself) credit it to be.<br /> <br /> The ability to &quot;bend the laws of reality&quot; isn't an intellectual talent. There's no connection from <i>any</i> attribute to <i>the ability</i> to perform magick. A mage can reasonably have any spread of attribute dots based on 7/5/3 and that's perfectly fine.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hahaha...IQ 100 is above mine? My dear kid, I'm a recognized gifted individual and I've been working with gifted people for quite some years now, sorry to disappoint you, but my IQ is in the house of 140, depending on the test etc, not that it matters to the discussion, but you pathethically tried to offend me while I was just expressing my opinion with all due respect for the others who do not share such opinion... I didn't say IQ 100 is low, but average and I don't think an &quot;average person&quot; should be able to become a trully powerful Hermetic Mage or the like. Of course people like you could think of cheesy ways that would make it possible in a game. Just bear in mind that any &quot;commoner&quot; (such as the baker, the guard, or the waste collector etc...) is supposed to have a trait of 2 in Intelligence and only the trully &quot;mentally handcapped individuals&quot; would have a lower level than that. Average isn't &quot;smarter than most people&quot; like you stated, in fact your statement is very shallow and meaningless like most things you say and unsurprisingly didn't add anything to the discussion.<br /> <br /> Cheers,<br /> Daniel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T00:12:30-08:00","id":1001232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1000608-mage-intelligence?p=1001207#post1001207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hahaha...IQ 100 is above mine?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, step back and reread.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2367_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2367\" data-vbnamecard=\"2367\">Resplendent Fire</a> didn't say anything about your IQ. They said that an IQ of 100 is smarter than you're acknowledging it to be.<br /> <br /> If anything you're just making their point. Having an IQ isn't the same thing as being &quot;smart.&quot; It doesn't determine if you're going to apply critical reading skills, or stoop to getting offended to justify being obnoxious.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...I don't think an &quot;average person&quot; should be able to become a trully powerful Hermetic Mage or the like. </div> </div> </div>By definition, average people don't become mages. That's why mages have above average Attributes and above average Willpower. All mage PCs are exceptional people.<br /> <br /> However, mages don't all have to be above average in a single express of character aptitude. If you've seriously spent time working with gifting individuals, you'd know that intelligence expresses itself in a large number of ways that are not all covered by the Intelligence trait in the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just bear in mind that any &quot;commoner&quot; (such as the baker, the guard, or the waste collector etc...) is supposed to have a trait of 2 in Intelligence and only the trully &quot;mentally handcapped individuals&quot; would have a lower level than that. Average isn't &quot;smarter than most people&quot; like you stated, </div> </div> </div>Wow.<br /> <br /> OK.<br /> <br /> First off, occupation does not dictate intelligence. It is not uncommon for highly intelligent people to seek ways to hide their intellect because as children it is often a primary source of ostracization and social anxiety. Having an occupation that might not be mentally stimulating can be emotionally safe, while they exercise their minds in comfortable settings (esp. in modern times where they can use the Internet as an outlet) via hobbies.<br /> <br /> Second, an Intelligence of 1 does not indicate a mental handicap. It represents &quot;below average,&quot; there's a fairly big range between being below the literal average of 100, and having a low enough IQ to be considered to have a mental handicap. And actual handicap, disability, or so on would be a flaw, not a 1.<br /> <br /> Remember, between a character with Intelligence 1/Computers 5, Intelligence 3/Computers 3, and Intelligence 5/Computers 1, the only difference mechanically is the when a specialty will apply to Int + Computer rolls. Int 1/Ability 5 isn't someone with a handicap, they're someone that's dedicated hard work perfecting their learned skills in spite of not being the brightest in the class.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 11-10-2016, 03:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T01:24:15-08:00","id":1001247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1000608-mage-intelligence?p=1001232#post1001232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dude, step back and reread.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2367_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2367\" data-vbnamecard=\"2367\">Resplendent Fire</a> didn't say anything about your IQ. They said that an IQ of 100 is smarter than you're acknowledging it to be.<br /> <br /> If anything you're just making their point. Having an IQ isn't the same thing as being &quot;smart.&quot; It doesn't determine if you're going to apply critical reading skills, or stoop to getting offended to justify being obnoxious.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> By definition, average people don't become mages. That's why mages have above average Attributes and above average Willpower. All mage PCs are exceptional people.<br /> <br /> However, mages don't all have to be above average in a single express of character aptitude. If you've seriously spent time working with gifting individuals, you'd know that intelligence expresses itself in a large number of ways that are not all covered by the Intelligence trait in the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Wow.<br /> <br /> OK.<br /> <br /> First off, occupation does not dictate intelligence. It is not uncommon for highly intelligent people to seek ways to hide their intellect because as children it is often a primary source of ostracization and social anxiety. Having an occupation that might not be mentally stimulating can be emotionally safe, while they exercise their minds in comfortable settings (esp. in modern times where they can use the Internet as an outlet) via hobbies.<br /> <br /> Second, an Intelligence of 1 does not indicate a mental handicap. It represents &quot;below average,&quot; there's a fairly big range between being below the literal average of 100, and having a low enough IQ to be considered to have a mental handicap. And actual handicap, disability, or so on would be a flaw, not a 1.<br /> <br /> Remember, between a character with Intelligence 1/Computers 5, Intelligence 3/Computers 3, and Intelligence 5/Computers 1, the only difference mechanically is the when a specialty will apply to Int + Computer rolls. Int 1/Ability 5 isn't someone with a handicap, they're someone that's dedicated hard work perfecting their learned skills in spite of not being the brightest in the class.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> First of all you got me wrong in almost everyway conceivable. In second place I'm really tired after a day at the University with several classes, discussions, seminar etc andI have no time to waste with trolls. I have really read quickly and thought he was provoking me, if that wasn't his intent, then I apologize for the episode as I obviously didn't use it to justify my response, I really thought that was his intention, besides english isn't my first, or even second language.<br /> <br /> &quot;Being Smart&quot; doesn't mean anything by itself. There are indeed several types of intelligence, or at least that's usually the standard interpretation nowadays (or should I say since the late 80s, after Gardener developed his theory of multiple intelligences listing his famous 9 types of intelligence etc). I don't see the need deepen into this subject, but I just need to clarify that I fully understand (and agree, because of course I could not agree, there are always different interpretations after all etc) that IQ isn't the only, and I'd say arguably not even the most important aspect of a person's &quot;intelligence&quot;, as there are other types of intelligence, like the &quot;polemic&quot; bodily-kinesthetic intelligence, that is linked to very talented athletes etc. But that doesn't mean much when we're talking about a game where you need to have points to justify your capacity to do things.<br /> <br /> What you're implying here is that the character doesn't need to have any kind of attribute to justify his actions and roleplaying, which I see as utterly pointless then to have a list of attributes etc, as you (in the case, the player) could use any cheap argument (like the ones you're using here) to basically tell that the character doesn't need any said requirement to achieve something.<br /> <br /> Then, finally you're trying to imply that I meant that occupations dictate intelligence or anything like that. That's very low of you, as I didn't say this, I just meant that the &quot;normal folk&quot;, not the mages or the &quot;night creatures&quot;, &quot;exceptional people&quot; like you wrote, have a &quot;standard&quot; of 2 in every attribute. So, all in all, if you think a mage doesn't need any kind of exceptional attribute to justify what they are, I'd say you're just using arguments to &quot;cheat&quot; the system and that's not how it works. We need to have the &quot;points on the sheet&quot; to tell what you're able to do or not, it's very simple, just as in any other game. But, if you think that in your game an hermetic mage could be a completelly illiterate with an intelligence below average, that's your problem, but I assure you that it's not how it should be.<br /> <br /> Cheers,<br /> Daniel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T01:29:59-08:00","id":1001249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1000608-mage-intelligence?p=1001066#post1001066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shamans are the intellectual elite of their cultures. &amp;quot;Witches,&amp;quot; at least competent ones, know a lot of herbal lore. There is a substantial intellectual component to martial arts.<br /> <br /> Heavy Arms mentioned a charity-minded Chorister, and I kind of get that. Except that almost anyone who does charity work on the level of organizing other people and making a large difference--aka anyone who is <i>exceptional</i> at what they are doing, as a mage should be--is going to be smarter than average.</div> </div> </div> </div> Intelligence is not knowledge, and elite could just as easily be a social thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T01:31:17-08:00","id":1001250,"title":"","content":"Do the same Intelligence test twice and suddenly you are more intelligent?<br /> No, your knowledge increased.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":12022,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","user":"Nonsense","date":".  Digital hickup 11-10-2016, 04:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T01:31:56-08:00","id":1001251,"title":"","content":"One thing I recall noticing when reading the Tradition books: most of the characters with average intelligence tend to mention something about them using stuff other Mages invented. I noticed this, irrc, when reading the Sons of Ether Trad book. I think the idea is, your power to wield magic is entirely about Arete, but it's mostly the smarties who are inventing truly new gadgets and rituals. Average intellect characters mostly just parrot what they've been taught, but can be as powerful or more so when doing that parroting. The Mage with the Arete of 4/Intelligence 2 may need to be taught how to wave his wand in a particular pattern or how to use an energy-pistol, but he'll still be more powerful than the the Arete 3/Intelligence 5 guy who invented it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T01:39:03-08:00","id":1001252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1000608-mage-intelligence?p=1001249#post1001249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Intelligence is not knowledge, and elite could just as easily be a social thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Surely, but then again we need to remember that one of the most characteristically inherent quality of intelligence is that it measures the capacity for learning new things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T01:42:07-08:00","id":1001254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1000608-mage-intelligence?p=1001252#post1001252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Surely, but then again we need to remember that one of the most characteristically inherent quality of intelligence is that it measures the capacity for learning new things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly true, in Mage this is a function of Experience. In RL you are right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T01:50:25-08:00","id":1001257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1000608-mage-intelligence?p=1001254#post1001254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not exactly true, in Mage this is a function of Experience. In RL you are right.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Haha good one! But really, I meant not in exactly game terms, but instead interpretting how should a character learn new knowledges etc. I as a storyteller would give advantage for a character with higher inteligence to learn things somehow faster, although it's hard to measure it systematically talking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T02:03:33-08:00","id":1001261,"title":"","content":"I don't recall where I read it, but it is stated that a new ability can be learned in X-Int days (I believe X is 6).<br /> <br /> Another thing from Seasonal learning in GttT is that each success from Int+Library cuts the time requirement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T02:07:56-08:00","id":1001262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1000608-mage-intelligence?p=1001247#post1001247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all you got me wrong in almost everyway conceivable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing you've said in the rest of this post really seems to support this. The only thing I failed to do was psychically intuit things about your current mental state I have no idea of knowing. You've provided nothing to indicate that I misinterpreted the text you wrote; just that you have realized that what you said was not what you should have said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In second place I'm really tired after a day at the University with several classes, discussions, seminar etc andI have no time to waste with trolls. </div> </div> </div>Then sleep on a post. If you're too tired to read a short five sentence post fully - even in a language that is not your first - then don't respond right away. The forum will be here after some rest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What you're implying here is that the character doesn't need to have any kind of attribute to justify his actions and roleplaying, </div> </div> </div>I have implied no such thing (implying is something I do when I state something). And I do not follow your reasoning for why you think it is justified for you to infer that this is what I meant (that's what you do with my statement).<br /> <br /> I have made no argument that characters do not need traits appropriate to their RP. I've the core of what I've stated is that, the Intelligence Attribute does not cover everything we call &quot;intelligence&quot; or &quot;being smart,&quot; or whatever, and that a character can be exceptionally good at something without being exceptional in the Intelligence Attribute.<br /> <br /> There is no connection between this stance, and the strawman you have constructed. The fact that I am comfortable with a character with exceptional Wits and average Intelligence being good at improvising tactics in the midst of a a battle because Wits is written to be more important than Intelligence in regards to quickly adapting decisions in fluid environments is not a rejection of the idea that a character should have stats to back up RP. It is a rejection of being overly restrictive of what those stats should be, or overly reliant on a single stat to govern RP.<br /> <br /> As the saying goes, there's more than one way to skin a cat, and there's more than one way to achieve a &quot;smart&quot; decision in RP from a variety of possible stats reinforced directions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then, finally you're trying to imply that I meant that occupations dictate intelligence or anything like that. </div> </div> </div>That's close to what you said. You post posited a correlation of occupation and intelligence. If that's not what you meant, please clarify instead of accusing me of bad faith posting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...I just meant that the &quot;normal folk&quot;, not the mages or the &quot;night creatures&quot;, &quot;exceptional people&quot; like you wrote, have a &quot;standard&quot; of 2 in every attribute. </div> </div> </div>Is assumption is faulty.<br /> <br /> &quot;Normal&quot; people in the game are like normal people. They range. They <u>average</u> at 2 for Attributes, across the population. Any given &quot;normal&quot; person in the WoD may be below, near/at, or above average despite being &quot;normal.&quot;<br /> <br /> The only purpose a default &quot;standard&quot; of 2 in every Attribute serves is as a game play abstraction for minor NPCs to be statted up/used more quickly by not having to remember nine different ratings. It has never been presented in the books as what most people would look like if you detailed each one fully, because far more people would deviate from average in every Attribute than people would hit all 2s.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, all in all, if you think a mage doesn't need any kind of exceptional attribute to justify what they are, I'd say you're just using arguments to &quot;cheat&quot; the system and that's not how it works. </div> </div> </div>I see no merit in your argumentation. Mages don't need any kind of exceptional Attribute to justify what they are. Awakening to being a mage is not predicated on Attributes, or the game would require specific Attributes since all mages would need to have them to have awakened. The only thing all mages have to have is will, which is why the game does ensure that all mages have above average Willpower at creation.<br /> <br /> I'm not cheating the system, because the system doesn't say I can't play an Intelligence 1 mage. The game directly allows this as a character option. There is no rule in the game that says I have to put any dots in Intelligence if I don't think it fits my character concept.<br /> <br /> You have very significantly failed to demonstrate that this is not how &quot;it&quot; works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But, if you think that in your game an hermetic mage could be a completelly illiterate with an intelligence below average, that's your problem, but I assure you that it's not how it should be. </div> </div> </div>I don't recall saying anything of the sort, and I in fact said quite the opposite in my first post as the Hermetics are a Tradition who's philosophy is strenuously academic. I do think an Intelligence 1 Hermetic is doable (esp. with the less academic focused houses like Flambeau), but it would certainly need to be backed up with Abilities to justify the Hermetics bothering with someone with below average Intelligence due to the groups cultural biases.<br /> <br /> This, of course, has nothing to do with mages as a whole though, because not all mages are Hermetics who are expected to put up with the rigorous training in the humanities and the occult that goes with that Tradition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T04:05:48-08:00","id":1001295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1000608-mage-intelligence?p=1001247#post1001247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> First of all you got me wrong in almost everyway conceivable. In second place I'm really tired after a day at the University with several classes, discussions, seminar etc andI have no time to waste with trolls. I have really read quickly and thought he was provoking me, if that wasn't his intent, then I apologize for the episode as I obviously didn't use it to justify my response, I really thought that was his intention, besides english isn't my first, or even second language.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't trying to provoke you. I was <i>disagreeing with you.</i> Disagreement isn't provocation, or at least shouldn't be. I am honestly puzzled as to how someone could take &quot;Average intelligence is smarter than you're giving credit for&quot; as provocation.<br /> <br /> Also, I am not a &quot;he&quot; or a &quot;him&quot; or a &quot;his.&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> Thank you. While I wouldn't have made quite the same arguments in quite the same way, if I tried to respond to anything I'd just be repeating points you made. Excellent posts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 11-10-2016, 07:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T04:43:17-08:00","id":1001308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1000608-mage-intelligence?p=1000696#post1000696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Good points. I see that for the general &quot;miracle worker&quot;, inteligence isn't that much of a requirement, so for that archetype it does make sense having a trait of 2 (or even &quot;omg duh&quot; intelligence 1) and still &quot;meet the requirement&quot;. In any case, I think that overall it's very cheesy for many kinds of characters to think intelligence 2 should be enough to get everything they want in game (players tend to not give a good priority to purchase attribube points with xp), besides, <b>Inteligence 2 is basically around (according to the books at least) Iq 100 or so, don't get me wrong, but it's a bit hard for me to imagine many teachers with such low iq</b>, let alone &quot;Wizards who can bend the laws of reality itself&quot;.<br /> <br /> Cheers,<br /> Daniel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quoting you saying what you said you didn't say.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1000608-mage-intelligence?p=1001207#post1001207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hahaha...IQ 100 is above mine? My dear kid, I'm a recognized gifted individual and I've been working with gifted people for quite some years now, sorry to disappoint you, but my IQ is in the house of 140, depending on the test etc, not that it matters to the discussion, but you pathethically tried to offend me while I was just expressing my opinion with all due respect for the others who do not share such opinion... I didn't say IQ 100 is low, but average and I don't think an &quot;average person&quot; should be able to become a trully powerful Hermetic Mage or the like. Of course people like you could think of cheesy ways that would make it possible in a game. Just bear in mind that any &quot;commoner&quot; (such as the baker, the guard, or the waste collector etc...) is supposed to have a trait of 2 in Intelligence and only the trully &quot;mentally handcapped individuals&quot; would have a lower level than that. Average isn't &quot;smarter than most people&quot; like you stated, in fact your statement is very shallow and meaningless like most things you say and unsurprisingly didn't add anything to the discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. I didn't say anything about <i>your</i> IQ. I said &quot;average for humans is smarter than most people (like yourself) credit it to be.&quot; Not smarter than you, smarter than you credit it to be.<br /> 2. I am not a &quot;kid.&quot;<br /> 3. You say you didn't say IQ 100 is low, but go read that bolded bit above because you absolutely <i>did</i> say IQ 100 is low.<br /> 4. &quot;People like me&quot; ran a successful Mage chronicle for several years. I think I've got some clues about how the game works without cheesing everything.<br /> 5. If you really believe that mages can't be of average intelligence, find some supporting quotes. You won't, because <i>they don't exist</i>.<br /> 6. As Heavy Gear pointed out, &quot;mentally handicapped individuals&quot; would have a flaw. Intelligence of 1 is simply below average intelligence. Probably one standard deviation below average, which isn't a sign of intellectual disability.<br /> 7. Your IQ is not really relevant to this conversation. No one questioned your intelligence. I only questioned your <i>conclusions</i>. And I still do, because your conclusions are questionable and not supported in the text.<br /> 8. I didn't say anything about an &quot;average person&quot; becoming a truly powerful Hermetic Mage. I said that a mage with <i>any distribution of attribute points</i> can be viable. A mage with <i>any distribution of attribute points</i> is above average with a 7/5/3 spread at <i>minimum.</i> They just might not be above average in intelligence.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T06:37:33-08:00","id":1001334,"title":"","content":"I feel kind of responsible for this, I shouldn't have brought it up. Sorry guys. I need to accept that my house rules are only of interest to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T09:28:36-08:00","id":1001381,"title":"","content":"trying to compare D&amp;D wizards to mages is not really going to work very well. the metaphysics do not mesh seeing as how D&amp;D is built for play balance and damage per level while mage is built for taking the tapestry of reality and making it into a boat or a hat or a flower. it does not matter how intelligent a person is when their avatar wakes up and power is thrust into their hands. it makes not a whiff of difference if they can understand complex quantum theory or euclidean geometry. all that stuff comes later when they get training and indoctrination into their tradition or convention. there is an interesting element of struggle for a character who awakened in a moment of crisis and finds themselves surrounded by magi who awakened through study and enlightenment that should not be ignored. the scorn that would be heaped on them would be fierce. their journey difficult and very much in the themes of mage. I think those arguing mages should default with high intelligence dismiss the path of growth a starting character can go through. don't forget awakenings are vastly different. sometimes they happen through a sudden epiphany and sometimes through a moment of determination where the persons very soul shouts out &quot;I refuse to let this happen&quot;<br /> now if you want to talk about rank and privilege then its fairly obvious that smarter more intelligent mages have clear advantages on their path of advancement in power and politics. intelligence mages will survive longer in danger and advance quicker in the ranks of the awakened. they will be more prevalent in the long term, more respected and visible. but they are not the be all end all of the magi. mages are human and humans are vastly varied","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>there are no bad ideas, just ideas that have not been refined enough","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1608-iamthesweeper","name":"IAmTheSweeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T13:20:01-08:00","id":1001457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1000608-mage-intelligence?p=1001334#post1001334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel kind of responsible for this, I shouldn't have brought it up. Sorry guys. I need to accept that my house rules are only of interest to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Don't feel responsible for anything, friend. It wasn't your fault, it's just that sometimes discussions go out of hand, specially when it comes down to sensitive matters such as this (even more so when people put bad faith in your words etc). <br /> <br /> Now to the &quot;folks&quot; united against me...<br /> <br /> Perhaps you got me wrong when I said that &quot;it's hard to imagine many teachers (professors in the case would be more fitting) with such a &quot;low iq&quot;, I didn't mean iq 100 is inherently low, as it is not, it's the average, but what I meant is that for some professions/occupations it's perhaps not enough to be &quot;average&quot;, so what I should have said was that I consider intelligence 2 to be low for an intellectual professional (of course this is very subjective, but that is another discussion). All in all, we're talking about a game, not real life, so I think that it's fair to consider that we need to simplify this kind of things a little. So that a trully dedicated &quot;intellectual professional&quot; in a game should deserve more than the &quot;average free points&quot; of a given attribute and that's the whole point of my argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T13:28:55-08:00","id":1001462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1000608-mage-intelligence?p=1001247#post1001247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> First of all you got me wrong in almost everyway conceivable. In second place I'm really tired after a day at the University with several classes, discussions, seminar etc andI have no time to waste with trolls.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">\u200bThe proper procedure when it comes to someone you believe is trolling you is to report the post, not make a retaliatory post. Since you did and I issued you a warning on another post for similar behavior our system has generated an automatic suspension. If/when you return you are expected to abide by the forum's rules and I suggest reading them before posting again.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T01:28:08-08:00","id":1001670,"title":"","content":"&quot;Intelligence&quot; is more than just your Attribute by that name, it also includes your other Mental Attributes and your Knowledge skills. I'd expect that most <i>established </i>magi/technocrats, regardless of their faction or other talents, would eventually put a fairly hefty investment into knowledge skills associated with their magical/enlightened practice.<br /> <br /> But 0xp characters are generally considered college-graduate aged, in their mid 20s or so. They need and have LOTS of room to grow as characters before they're considered established. They're basically just out of whatever passed for apprenticeship in their tradition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}